## What happened

Rigetti Computing (RGTI) has bounced from the daily 200-MA area and reclaimed the $20 level.

That is the first important technical improvement. The stock had been testing a major longer-term moving average, and buyers have now pushed it back above a round-number level that traders are likely watching.

The key point now is simple: **RGTI needs to close above $20 and defend it as support**.

A break above $20 is constructive, but it is not confirmation by itself. The setup becomes cleaner if the stock can hold above that level after the move, especially with earnings directly in focus.

If RGTI closes above $20 and then builds support there, the daily MA200 bounce has a stronger chance of turning into a higher-range recovery setup.

## Why it matters

Rigetti Computing is a quantum computing company focused on superconducting quantum processors, quantum cloud services and full-stack quantum computing systems.

That makes RGTI one of the more speculative pure-play quantum stocks. The company is not being valued only on current revenue. It is being valued on whether investors believe quantum computing can move from research and early contracts into real commercial adoption.

The timing matters because Rigetti is due to report Q1 2026 results after market close on May 11. Market coverage has highlighted that options traders are pricing in a large post-earnings move, with TipRanks reporting an expected move of about 16.9% around the report. :contentReference[oaicite:0]{index=0}

That means the $20 reclaim is happening right before a major catalyst. Traders are not just watching the chart. They are also positioning around earnings risk, quantum sector sentiment and whether Rigetti can show better commercial traction.

