## Levels to watch

- Support: $20 is the key level RGTI needs to close above and defend as new support.
- Resistance: The next resistance zone is the recent post-bounce supply above $20, where sellers may test whether the reclaim has real demand behind it.
- Moving averages: Daily MA200 is the main trend reference for this setup.
- Risk point: A failed close above $20, or a close above $20 followed by a quick loss of that level, would weaken the daily MA200 bounce.

## What would confirm the idea

The cleanest confirmation would be RGTI closing above $20 and then holding that level on the next pullback.

That would show buyers are not just chasing the first move off the daily MA200. It would show they are willing to defend the reclaim and treat $20 as a new support zone.

Volume matters here. A close above $20 with stronger volume would be more convincing than a quiet drift above the level.

The stronger version of the setup would be RGTI holding $20 through the earnings reaction, staying above the daily MA200, and then pushing into the next supply area without immediately rejecting.

That would suggest the market is starting to price the stock as a stronger quantum recovery setup rather than just a short-term bounce.

## What would weaken the idea

The setup weakens if RGTI fails to close above $20 or closes above it and then quickly loses the level.

That would suggest the breakout did not attract enough demand. It would also make the daily MA200 bounce look less reliable.

The bigger warning would be a move back below the daily MA200 with heavy volume. That would show the market is rejecting the recovery attempt and that sellers are still controlling the broader daily structure.

The setup would also weaken if earnings disappoint or if the company fails to show progress on revenue, bookings, customer demand or commercialization. Rigetti has had contract wins, but investors still need evidence that those wins are becoming a larger and more repeatable revenue base.

## Bull vs bear scenarios

**Bullish scenario:**  
RGTI closes above $20, holds that level as support, and stays constructive around the daily MA200. If earnings show better commercial momentum, stronger revenue visibility or useful customer traction, buyers may continue treating the stock as a high-beta quantum recovery name.

**Bearish scenario:**  
RGTI fails to hold $20, loses the daily MA200 area, and the earnings reaction turns into a failed reclaim. In that case, investors may refocus on small current revenue, ongoing losses, commercialization risk and the long timeline before quantum computing becomes widely profitable.

## Bottom line

RGTI has made an important short-term improvement by bouncing from the daily MA200 and reclaiming $20.

The setup now depends on confirmation. A close above $20 and a successful hold would support the recovery case; a failed reclaim would make the move look more like a short-term earnings-positioning bounce than a confirmed trend repair.
